 on I want to be the guy is  a game known for its difficulty I want  to be the boshy is an even more  difficult to remake made because  somebody thought the original game was  - easy this runner is playing the last  game on hard while attempting to  complete a 100% speed run this run is  epic not just because the streamer  witwix team rolls through all the stages  where most of us would have a hard time  getting through one but because he's so  damn entertaining to casually chatting  the whole way through while totally  smashing a famously brutal game at  breakneck speeds this Runner is all  kinds of awesome not to mention it's  probably the early opportunity I have to  see the end of this game The Legend of  Zelda Ocarina of Time isn't I want to be  the boshy hot but it certainly would be  difficult to play a blindfolded a feat  this next runner attempted through the  first three dungeon it's seriously cool  to see how much the runner run a guy  2489 knows about where he is in the game  just by listening to the surprisingly  detailed and varied sounds of ocarina of  time it's also fascinating to hear run a  guy tell the story about how he helped a  blind friend play a tape and decided in  the process to figure out how to play it  without the use of sight not only does  he successfully navigate the three  dungeons runnerguy is also able to  successfully execute a bunch of  difficult to activate glitches which  requires specific and frame-perfect  moves all while blindfolded this run is  madness awesome or inspiring madness  finally and this one is probably popped  up on your radar already since it's  sitting at half a million views on  YouTube is Kevin Delia's tetris the  grand master run playing on tgm3 master  mode where the speed and difficulty is  drastically increased runner Kevin DDR  plays the classic puzzle games so well  you feel ashamed to even consider trying  your amateur hand at it well maybe  that's just me although the ridiculously  speedy run culminating in level 999 is  phenomenal in and of itself the best bit  actually occurs during the credits of  the game here Kevin DDR flexes his  tetris skills by successfully planting  blocks on an invisible game board where  he can't see what he's doing it really  needs to be  seen to properly appreciate how  ridiculously clever this speedrunner is  let me know down in the comments which  of these runs was your favorite or if it  was a whole other run entirely for the  full runs you can head to the games done  quick YouTube or twitch page and  congrats to them for raising over one  and a half million dollars for charity I  will see you next week

